WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.040
In the year 548, the general Hou Jing, who had once surrendered to the Liang, suddenly betrayed the court and raised a rebellion.

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:11.942
He led his troops southward all the way, unstoppable.

00:00:12.292 --> 00:00:21.340
His rebel army soon marched on the capital Jiankang, and the people in the city were all thrown into panic, not knowing what to do.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:31.170
But the Liang imperial clansmen distrusted one another and guarded against each other; none was willing to send troops to rescue the capital.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:40.088
Before long, Hou Jing broke through Taicheng and seized control of the court; the great power of government fell into the rebels' hands.

00:00:40.438 --> 00:00:50.590
The flames of war spread; places all over Jiangnan suffered serious destruction, and many people were displaced, with no home to return to.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:01:00.252
This terrible Hou Jing Rebellion made the once-prosperous Liang dynasty decline swiftly, never to be what it had been.

